From 0dffc7fc0ee30d2026e922e8a5df7dddf9adbdcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:58:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs(mcp): camcraft-mcp skill row for
 electrode_from_faces

Adds the electrode_from_faces row (#1156) to the camcraft-mcp skill:
parameters, the undersize/condition rule, the burn fields it answers
with, and its refusals. Bumps PROCESS_VERSION to 53 (skill is a process file).

Fixes #1356

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
---
 .claude/PROCESS_VERSION              | 2 +-
 .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION b/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION
index 0691f67b2..59343b09e 100644
--- a/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION
+++ b/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION
@@ -1 +1 @@
-52
+53
diff --git a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
index 7c5db906c..11da3b8ed 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@ The server exposes tools across three modules in `crates/app/src/mcp/` (see `cra
 - `list_operation_types {}`: Inspect all supported operation types, parameter schemas, defaults, and compatible tool types.
 - `add_operation { "kind": string, "tool"?: string, "name"?: string, "source"?: string, "params"?: object }`: Add an operation to the active setup. `source` is `"stock"` (the default) or a model name. `tool` is required except for a kind that mounts no library tool (`list_operation_types` lists `"mounts_tool": false` and a note - today the Wire Contour): omit it there; naming one is refused by the command.
 - **Wire Contour (#532, #1108)**: a 2-axis wire EDM cut of one closed profile (a model's through silhouette or picked edges). Mount a wire EDM first - `load_machine { "path": "<.mch>" }` with an `edm.conditions` table (no library wire EDM exists until #533). Then `add_operation { "kind": "Wire Contour", "source": "<model>", "params": { "condition": "<condition id>", "side": "die"|"punch", "start": [x, y] } }` with no `tool` (fields: `top_z`, `bottom_z`, `condition`, `side`, `start`). `edit_operation` patches `side`, `start` and `condition`. Refusals arrive as tool errors in the command's words: a tool named, no or unknown condition, a condition with no gap or wire diameter; the start hole and the corner minimum are refused at `generate`. Not exercised on a real EDM control: the wire post is #533 and the program gate refuses a wire cut until it lands, so `post` fails by name.
+- **Sinker electrode (#547, #1156)**: `electrode_from_faces { "name": string, "picks": [face ids], "undersize"?: number, "condition"?: string, "setup"?: string, "orbit"?: number, "stub": number, "pickup": number }` generates a sinker EDM electrode from the picked faces of a cavity (its level floor and every vertical wall standing on it, `face:0x…` ids from `list_features`, all on one model) and adds it as a document tool. Give `undersize` (mm per side, 0 or more) or `condition` (a machine EDM condition id, read from the setup's sinker EDM; `setup` names that setup, default the active one), not both; `stub` (more than 0) is how far the electrode stands above the cavity's mouth; `pickup` (0 or more) is the offset from the electrode's top to the measuring reference. `orbit` makes it that much smaller again per side. The reply gives the electrode, its `burn` fields (the `add_operation` params of a Sinker Burn of this cavity) and a `warning` when the undersize is unusual. Only an axis-aligned rectangular cavity yields an electrode; refused by name: picks on more than one model or on something that is not a face, a degenerate face, a boss, rib or overhang standing in the electrode's way, a condition with no undersize or no sinker EDM setup, and malformed numbers. One undo step.
 - `edit_operation { "name": string, "params": object }`: JSON merge-patch operation parameters (e.g. `stepdown`, `stepover`, `feed`, `spindle_speed`).
 - `delete_operation { "name": string }`: Remove an operation and invalidate its cached toolpath.
 - `rename_operation { "name": string, "new_name": string }`: Change an operation's display name (1-120 printable characters). Its stable key and its place in the program do not change; naming it back to its key clears the display name. Names are unique and cannot take another operation's key. One undo step.

